    "diagnosis": "ALK-positive anaplastic large cell lymphoma",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "Classic morphology, characterized by a variable number of characteristic hallmark cells with abundant cytoplasm and large horseshoe-shaped nuclei and multiple nucleoli (&lt;&lt;31023&gt;&gt;). Small cell pattern, demonstrating depletion of background lymphoid cells. The neoplastic cells are predominantly small in size, with eosinophilic cytoplasm (&lt;&lt;31024&gt;&gt;). Lymphohistiocytic pattern, characterized by numerous histiocytes admixed with atypical lymphoid cells, some showing vacuolated cytoplasm (&lt;&lt;31025&gt;&gt;). Monomorphic pattern, comprising uniform large to medium-sized cells (&lt;&lt;31027&gt;&gt;).",
    "source": "Kojo S.J. Elenitoba-Johnson",
    "copyright": "",
